          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ঘনিয়ে আসা — ghôniye āsā — \"to draw near (of a date or danger)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বিয়ের দিন ঘনিয়ে এল। Biyer din ghôniye elô. The wedding day drew near."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): সেই দিন ঘনিয়ে এল, sei din ghôniye elô."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ঘনিয়ে আসা (ghôniye āsā) joins ঘনিয়ে, the -এ form of a verb built on ঘন, \"dense, close\", to আসা, \"to come\": coming closer and closer. CDIAL lists Bengali ghana, \"thick, dense\", under Sanskrit ghana, and notes a Bengali verb from it meaning to come close (CDIAL 4424)."
            }
          ]
        },
